{
  "tema": 5962,
  "slug": "por-causa-razon-gracias-por",
  "titulo": "Por (not para) for cause or reason",
  "subtitulo": "«Gracias por todo.»",
  "foto": "t05.jpg",
  "regla": "Use por to give the cause or reason behind something: what made it happen (because of, due to, on account of). Para looks forward to a goal; por looks back to a cause.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Por** + noun, pronoun or infinitive gives the **cause**: _because of_, _due to_, _for_."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "result",
            "+ por +",
            "cause"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Common uses: **gracias por**, **perdón por**, **por la lluvia**, **por el tráfico**, **por eso** (_that's why_)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "With people, **por** means _because of_ or _for the sake of_: **lo hice por ti** = _I did it because of you / for you_. (**Lo hice para ti** is a different idea: _I made it for you_, as a gift.)"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "With an infinitive, **por** gives the action that caused it: **me multaron por manejar rápido** (_they fined me for speeding_)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Para** is different: it points **forward** to a goal or a receiver. Ask yourself: is this the reason (**por**) or the purpose (**para**)?"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **por** looks in the rearview mirror (what caused it); **para** looks through the windshield (where it's going)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "==Gracias por== tu ayuda.",
              "en": "Thanks for your help."
            },
            {
              "es": "Cancelaron el torneo ==por== la lluvia.",
              "en": "They cancelled the tournament because of the rain."
            },
            {
              "es": "Llegué tarde ==por== el tráfico en la línea.",
              "en": "I was late because of the traffic at the border."
            },
            {
              "es": "Me multaron ==por== manejar sin licencia.",
              "en": "They fined me for driving without a license."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Perdón por== la tardanza.",
              "en": "Sorry for being late."
            },
            {
              "es": "Estoy muerto ==por== el entrenamiento de ayer.",
              "en": "I'm wiped out from yesterday's training."
            },
            {
              "es": "Lo hice ==por== ti.",
              "en": "I did it for you (because of you)."
            },
            {
              "es": "Llovió toda la semana; ==por eso== no surfeamos.",
              "en": "It rained all week; that's why we didn't surf."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
